``` Failed Login Brute Force
    Purpose : Flag a source that fails to log on many times in a short window.
    Data    : Windows Security log, EventCode 4625 (failed logon).
    Controls: AC-7, AU-6, SI-4  (see data/detections_to_controls.csv)
    Tuning  : Raise the threshold for shared jump hosts or VPN concentrators.
              Exclude known vulnerability scanners by source address.
    Example environment: Harborlight Logistics (fictional). ```
index=wineventlog sourcetype="WinEventLog:Security" EventCode=4625
| bin _time span=10m
| stats count AS failures dc(TargetUserName) AS distinct_users values(TargetUserName) AS users BY _time, IpAddress, ComputerName
| where failures >= 10
| eval pattern=if(distinct_users >= 5, "possible password spray", "possible brute force")
| sort - failures
